              "type": "text",
              "text": "Daniel practises his guitar for 48 minutes every day.",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "break"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "How many days will it take him to log 10 000 hours of practice?",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$12\\,500$ days",
      "worked": "Let $x$ be the number of days. Convert the total practice time to minutes, then use equivalent rates.\n$$\\begin{align*}10\\,000\\text{ h}&=10\\,000\\times60\\text{ min}\\\\&=600\\,000\\text{ min}\\\\\\frac{48\\text{ min}}{1\\text{ day}}&=\\frac{600\\,000\\text{ min}}{x\\text{ days}}\\\\\\frac{1\\text{ day}}{48\\text{ min}}&=\\frac{x\\text{ days}}{600\\,000\\text{ min}}\\\\\\frac{600\\,000}{48}\\text{ days}&=x\\text{ days}\\\\x&=12\\,500\\end{align*}$$\nIt will take $12\\,500$ days.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 52
  },
